{
 "tensatory": "0.1",
 "name": "MNIST MLP: live PCA landscape",
 "summary": "The loss-landscape prototype's trained 784-256-256-10 MLP (269,322 parameters) evaluated IN THE BROWSER by the net evaluator: cross-entropy and accuracy on 1024 (or 256) training examples around θ* along the top-3 PCA directions of its SGD trajectory; weights, directions and data as .npz members; the prototype's PyTorch-sampled volume alongside for comparison.",
 "details": "From ~/projects/loss-landscape/out/mnist_mlp.pt (landscape.py: SGD with momentum, 3 epochs, 48 snapshots). The PCA directions are the top right-singular vectors of θ_t − θ* over the trajectory (explained variance 80.4%, 9.1%, 2.8%); the trajectory is projected onto them and θ* sits at the origin. The box is the one volume.py used for the 64³ volume (viewer/data/mnist_mlp_pca), whose every-other sample is vol.npy here, so `sampled/…` (PyTorch, N = 1024) and the live `loss` (the net evaluator, same 1024 examples) should agree to float32. `fast/…` uses the first 256 examples. Weights are float32 .npz members ([in, out]); the eval set is uint8 pixels, normalized inside the net. Generated by tools/mnist/export.py.",
